    {
      "id": "good-read-with-a-collection-addresses-that-file-not-the-entity-type",
      "steps": [
        {
          "event": "ROW_READ",
          "payload": {
            "key": "k",
            "entityType": "bad type!",
            "id": "a",
            "collection": "billing"
          },
          "from": "ready",
          "expect": {
            "emits": [
              {
                "event": "STORE_FAILED",
                "payload": {
                  "key": "k",
                  "message": "os/read-file: no os host configured"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "note": "EXEC-STORE-4: the file is named by the collection. Replay answers the file read with 'no os host configured' (effect args are not evaluated), so the proof is that the ask passes the file-name guard on the collection, where the same entity type without a collection is refused (control)"
    },
